-- title:
--   Hecke stability of the specialisation kernel for q ≠ ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ and assume `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar N`, i.e. the operators `heckeOperatorBar N` attached to any two primes commute on $J_0(N)$, where `JZero N` is $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field `modularFunctionFieldBar N` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid N$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, let `data : ModularPolynomialData ℓ` be a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(\ell)$ annihilating the pair $(j, j_\ell)$, and let `hKr` assert the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X^{\ell} - Y)(X - Y^{\ell})$ modulo $\ell$ in the bivariate reduction. Assume integrality of the ring homomorphisms `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` at level $N$ and prime $\ell$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that the residue field $k$ of $A$ has characteristic $\ell$ and is algebraically closed, and that `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, the subfield of $k((q))$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`, is a curve over $k$ (principal divisors of degree zero, finite residue extensions, and $\Omega$ free of rank one). Let $S$ be a `PlaceSpecialization` packet for $A$, $\ell$, $N$, `data`, `hKr` with target field $k$ and reduction map the residue map of $A$, so in particular $S$ provides a map `sp` on places and a group homomorphism `spPic0 : JZero N →+ Pic0 k (modularFunctionFieldC k N)`. Then for every prime $q \neq \ell$ and every $x \in$ `JZero N` with $S.\mathrm{spPic}^0(x) = 0$, one has $S.\mathrm{spPic}^0(\mathrm{heckeGen}\, q \cdot x) = 0$, the action being the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar N` and `heckeGen q` the polynomial variable indexed by $q$.
--
--   This is the statement that the kernel of the specialisation homomorphism from $J_0(N)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the characteristic-$\ell$ model is stable under the Hecke operator $T_q$ for every prime $q$ different from the residue characteristic. It is used, together with surjectivity of the specialisation map, in [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_heckeDescent_family_qne_ell`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.exists_heckeDescent_family_qne_ell) to descend the operators $T_q$, $q \neq \ell$, to the special fibre.
